      "threads": [
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "TradFi bank stablecoin entry",
          "why": "The top-clicked headlines are all institutional: Deutsche Bank on UDPN, BBVA partnering with Visa, BofA and Stripe joining the race — readers are tracking which legacy names blink first."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Reserve rules and regulatory frameworks",
          "why": "The Lummis-Gillibrand Act, BIS warnings, Canada's par-redemption mandate, and IMF run-risk alerts drew sustained clicks, signaling readers want to know who sets the rules before picking winners."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Legacy rail displacement milestones",
          "why": "Volume comparisons — stablecoins topping Visa in 2024 and flipping ACH at $7.2T — framed as concrete proof points that readers treat as scoreboard updates on an ongoing race."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Emerging-market card adoption",
          "why": "StraitsX's 83x card-issuance surge in Southeast Asia and dtcpay's Series A show readers tracking where stablecoins are already invisibly embedded in daily commerce rather than still experimental."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Yield-bearing stablecoin risk",
          "why": "Plasma's 10%-yield card and the BIS warning that yield blurs payments with investment products attracted readers alert to the regulatory and run-risk landmine hiding inside 'interest-bearing stablecoins'."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "AI agent machine-to-machine payments",
          "why": "Galaxy's x402 research and Google's open-source AI payments protocol pulled readers curious about stablecoins becoming invisible HTTP-layer infrastructure for autonomous agents rather than a consumer product."
        }
      ]
    },
